# A part's lock (SEQ held on its screen, 600 ms): a new song keeps it. PLAY; ALGO to Drums, EDIT, SEQ held locks the
# drums (the padlock by its name; no re-roll waits: a hold never also re-rolls), a short SEQ there no longer re-rolls
# them; the main screen's drums tile shows the lock. SEQ there rolls a new song: the drums play as before (kit,
# pattern, kick, ride, variation), the other parts rolled anew, no block late. SEQ held again unlocks them, and the
# next song rolls the drums too. SAVE on a part's screen is the measures again, not a lock. On the main screen SEQ held
# locks the highlighted tile's part.
listen
wait 1400
tap PLAY
wait 3000
spin ALGO 1
tap EDIT
wait 50
said DRUMS, PAGE 1/2
# SAVE: the measures, as everywhere
tap SAVE
wait 50
said REDRAW
expect locks 0
# held 700 ms: locked, and no re-roll of the drums waits
press SEQ
wait 700
release SEQ
wait 50
said DRUMS LOCKED
expect locks 1
expect pending -1
shot drums-locked.png
# a short press: the drums' own re-roll, refused while locked
tap SEQ
wait 50
said DRUMS IS LOCKED
expect pending -1
tap HOME
wait 50
expect home 1
shot main-locked.png
remember
# a new song (after the gap: 2-4 s)
tap SEQ
wait 6000
expect songs 2
expect same_song 0
expect same_drums 1
expect parts_moved >2
expect late 0
# unlocked (back on its screen: a new song went home, the drums still highlighted), the next song rolls them too
tap EDIT
wait 50
press SEQ
wait 700
release SEQ
wait 50
said DRUMS UNLOCKED
expect locks 0
tap HOME
remember
tap SEQ
wait 6000
expect songs 3
expect same_song 0
expect same_drums 0
# on the main screen SEQ held locks the highlighted tile's part (the bass), with no new song; on the song's line a
# hold does nothing; a short SEQ there is a new song, which keeps the bass
spin ALGO 1
wait 50
press SEQ
wait 700
release SEQ
wait 50
said BASS LOCKED
expect locks 2
expect songs 3
shot main-hold-lock.png
spin ALGO -2
press SEQ
wait 700
release SEQ
wait 50
expect locks 2
expect songs 3
remember
tap SEQ
wait 6000
expect songs 4
expect same_song 0
expect same_bass 1
expect late 0
